# One-Click REST API Deployment

This project uses **Terraform** to deploy a REST API on AWS behind a Classic ELB with an Auto Scaling Group.  
It includes scripts for one‑click deployment, testing, and teardown.

---

## 🚀 Deployment Steps

1. Clone the repository:
   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/vsb1712/Devops-assignment.git
   cd Devops-assignment/terraform

terraform init
terraform apply -auto-approve
http://one-click-rest-api-elb-306287030.us-east-1.elb.amazonaws.com/

2.Testing Steps
Use the ELB DNS name from the output.

Test the root endpoint: http://one-click-rest-api-elb-306287030.us-east-1.elb.amazonaws.com/
Test the health endpoint: http://one-click-rest-api-elb-306287030.us-east-1.elb.amazonaws.com/health

Teardown Steps
To avoid AWS charges, destroy all resources when finished: terraform destroy -auto-approve


GitHub Actions Workflow (Optional)
You can automate deployment and teardown using GitHub Actions. Add a file .github/workflows/terraform.yml:

name: Terraform CI/CD

on:
  workflow_dispatch:   # manual trigger
  push:
    branches:
      - main

jobs:
  terraform:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

    steps:
      - name: Checkout code
        uses: actions/checkout@v3

      - name: Setup Terraform
        uses: hashicorp/setup-terraform@v2

      - name: Terraform Init
        run: terraform init

      - name: Terraform Plan
        run: terraform plan

      - name: Terraform Apply
        if: github.ref == 'refs/heads/main'
        run: terraform apply -auto-approve


Summary
Deploy: terraform apply -auto-approve

Test: curl http://<ELB_DNS_NAME>/ and /health

Teardown: terraform destroy -auto-approve

Optional CI/CD: GitHub Actions workflow for automated deployment

